  "plan": "```markdown\n# Kriya Planner Agent - Implementation Plan\n\n## Overview\nCreate a minimal Java 17 Maven application named `hello-kriya` that prints \"Hello from Kriya\", includes a unit test, and is runnable.\n\n## Files to Create/Modify\n\n### 1. Project Structure Setup\n- **pom.xml** - Maven configuration file (REQ-1, REQ-2)\n- **src/main/java/hellokriya/App.java** - Main application class (REQ-1, REQ-2)\n- **src/test/java/hellokriya/AppTest.java** - Unit test class (REQ-1)\n\n## Step-by-Step Implementation\n\n### Step 1: Create Maven Project Structure\n- Create `pom.xml` with Java 17 target and JUnit dependency (REQ-1, REQ-2)\n- Create directory structure for source and test code\n\n### Step 2: Implement Main Application\n- Create `src/main/java/hellokriya/App.java` with main method that prints \"Hello from Kriya\" (REQ-1, REQ-2)\n\n### Step 3: Add Unit Test\n- Create `src/test/java/hellokriya/AppTest.java` with basic test for the application (REQ-1)\n\n### Step 4: Verify Build and Execution\n- Confirm Maven build works correctly (REQ-2)\n- Verify application runs and outputs expected message (REQ-2)\n\n## Verification Steps\n- Run `mvn compile` to ensure compilation succeeds\n- Run `mvn test` to verify unit tests pass\n- Run `mvn exec:java` to confirm application executes properly\n\n```",
